I'd like to play with colored ascii characters on the nethack.alt.org
server, but I usually find myself dying stupid deaths because I can't
see the lightest colors very well (bright cyan in particular is damn
near impossible to pick out).  Is there a way to modify the default
colors through my nethackrc file so that I can make the lighter tones a
more visible color?

There's a brief reference to color in the nethack guidebook
(http://www.nethack.org/v343/Guidebook.html).  Here's what the
guidebook says (under the heading Platform-specific Customization
options):

videocolors
Set the color palette for PC systems using NO_TERMS (default
4-2-6-1-5-3-15-12-10-14-9-13-11, (PC NetHack only). The order of colors
is red, green, brown, blue, magenta, cyan, bright.white, bright.red,
bright.green, yellow, bright.blue, bright.magenta, and bright.cyan.
Cannot be set with the `O' command.

I tried adding the following line to my option file, but I get an error
when I start a new game:

OPTIONS=videocolors:4-2-6-1-5-3-15-12-10-14-9-13-3

Can someone steer me in the correct direction for fixing this problem?



